{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:9bca49fef1c50e1e","name":"EG-6 Power Droid","source":{"id":"source:reference-9bca49fef1c50e1e","title":"EG-6 Power Droid","revision":18904,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T20:57:07Z","sha256":"b743a2d50378912b642fc6bdaf226111071566ce3e36b3cab1b2f54a963ed5c2","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18904","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=EG-6%20Power%20Droid&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-9bca49fef1c50e1e","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Threats of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Threats_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The EG-6 Power Droid is one of the most recognizable ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"}," in the galaxy. Appearing as nothing more than a black box with short legs and no visible manipulators, the few people who are unaware of its function wonder why ",{"tag":"a","children":["Veril Line Systems"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Veril_Line_Systems","referenceId":"reference:99d42d8b7aa8c6f7"}," built it in the first place. Without Power Droids, however, modern society would grind to a halt. \n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Inside the walking black box sits a powerful fusion generator, which is well protected by its thick duranium exterior. The EG-6's only function is to provide power to machines of all sorts during times when a more permanent power source is not available or convenient, which has earned the Droid the nickname \"Walking Battery.\" In fact, the EG-6 is capable of recharging itself without needing to shut down, allowing it to function continuously. \n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The few embellishments the EG-6 has include a visual sensor with infrared capability and highly advanced diagnostic programming that allows the Droid to perform safety checks on the mechanism it is servicing. \n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["EG-6 Power Droids can be played as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Heroes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Heroes"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["EG-6 Power Droid Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["From the towering spires of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Coruscant"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Coruscant","referenceId":"reference:2ee37a21e9e7a955"}," to the moisture farms of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Tatooine"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tatooine","referenceId":"reference:a1b911e88e4876e1"}," and beyond, the EG-6 can be seen anywhere that technology exists. It is a common sight in ship hangars, repulsorcraft pools, and tech domes.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Even though the EG-6 is not a highly capable Droid by itself, it is useful for assisting other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"}," with their work. Astromech Droids have worked with a Power Droid that kept watch over the ship they are repairing to make sure that other systems do not unexpectedly create a mishap. Small military units and mercenary groups have put the EG-6 to use providing the energy needed to keep their heavy guns firing or giving emergency power to their ship in a time of crisis.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Despite the Droid's usefulness, its sheer stupidity has caused many a Power Droid to get away from its master and become lost. Such a Droid often gets picked up by local law enforcement if it's on a world in or near ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Core"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Core?action=edit&redlink=1"},", where its owner can reclaim it. If an EG-6 Droid gets lost on an Outer Rim world, on the other hand, scavengers usually claim it and either become its new master or sell it to some other needy party.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["EG-6 Power Droid Statistics (CL 0)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Small ",{"tag":"a","children":["5th-Degree Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/5th-Degree_Droid"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 1\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," -1; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Darkvision"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Darkvision"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," -1\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic (understand only), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Binary"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Binary","referenceId":"reference:ee1c8277caf5fb9b"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 18 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 18), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 12, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Will Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Will_Defense"},": 9\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},": 5, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Threshold"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Threshold"},": 12\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Immune:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Traits"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Traits"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Offense"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[